From df6dc8eda3b704a353df56533818dc1667b41ece Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dana Kovalenko <dana.kovalenko@example.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:48:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] eval grounding: baseline lift, --min-contexts, --annotate

`eval grounding` scored only the docs-arm answer, so a high grounding
score could not be told apart from a model that says the same things
without any docs. Score the without_docs answer against the same
retrieved context and report the difference as `lift`.

- `--min-contexts N` skips answers that retrieved fewer than N snippets;
  a single short snippet makes the overlap ratio noisy.
- `--annotate PATH` writes a copy of the answers file with a
  per-question `grounding` block, so downstream reports can read the
  score next to each answer instead of joining two files.
- answers.v1 declares the `grounding` block.
- Document the new flags next to the standalone pipeline commands.

Signed-off-by: Dana Kovalenko <dana.kovalenko@example.com>
---
